{"skill":{"slug":"git-workflows","displayName":"Git Workflows"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770158556308,"changelog":"Initial release: Interactive rebase, bisect, worktree, reflog recovery, cherry-pick, subtree/submodule, sparse checkout, conflict resolution, stash patterns, blame archaeology","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":13371,"sha256":"d469d22281d222d3cc7a32ea8dcd35b183aacd714e996918835099895d73c455","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1992,"sha256":"b4572bf89d9b9ccf7fe95e2d65ad27766cb1984f0523bb07a0b6539782599259","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031878208,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1a4e857f1803629dc06edbf5a20d31a5019bfa79a2b21f48f39f18bc19a7c253","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1a4e857f1803629dc06edbf5a20d31a5019bfa79a2b21f48f39f18bc19a7c253","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: git-workflows\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides extensive documentation and examples for advanced Git operations. All commands demonstrated are standard Git commands or common shell commands used in conjunction with Git (e.g., creating a temporary test script for `git bisect run`). There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent. The content is purely instructional and aligns with the stated purpose of teaching Git workflows.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161187829},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":52,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789031878208},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward Git workflow reference skill with some destructive command examples that users should run carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Repository mutation, network Git remotes, worktrees, and temporary scripts are proportionate to Git workflow guidance, though users should adapt paths and remotes to their own repositories.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single non-executable SKILL.md file with metadata requiring only git; no install scripts, bundled executables, dependencies, or hidden loaders were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are user-directed examples, not automatic execution, but they include destructive commands such as reset, stash clearing, submodule removal, and remote tag deletion with limited caution text.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill includes persistent Git configuration via git config --global rerere.enabled true and repository-altering commands, but no background services, privilege escalation, credential access, or cross-session agent behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is advanced Git workflows, and its content is a Markdown guide covering rebase, bisect, worktrees, reflog recovery, submodules, sparse checkout, conflicts, stash, blame, and tags.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an advanced Git command reference. Before running examples, read each command carefully, make backups or stashes before history-changing operations, double-check rm -rf paths and remotes, and avoid the fixed /tmp script pattern on shared machines.","findings":"[TM1] expected: The flagged reset and removal commands are real destructive operations, but they appear as explicit Git recovery and submodule examples aligned with the skill's purpose rather than hidden or automatic behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: The scanner's warning concern is valid as user guidance: reset --hard, rm -rf, and git stash clear should include stronger data-loss cautions, but the commands are disclosed and purpose-aligned.\n[T09] expected: The fixed /tmp test script path in the bisect example is a safer-coding issue in hostile multi-user environments; it is not evidence of malicious behavior, but users should prefer mktemp or a trusted repo-local script.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031878208}}}}}